Build the configurable machine into the ppc64 target too.

meson's `when:` keys only name a target's own architecture (TARGET_PPC64 for
ppc64-softmmu); TARGET_PPC, its base architecture, reaches config-target.h but
not those conditions.  So the TARGET_PPC line below left ppc64 without the
"configurable" machine SmallWorld runs PowerPC on, the same way aarch64 and
x86_64 needed their own lines.  configurable_machine.c itself is written
against TARGET_PPC, which ppc64 does define.

Generated on top of panda-qemu-superh.patch, which adds the TARGET_SH4 line.

--- a/hw/avatar/meson.build
+++ b/hw/avatar/meson.build
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 ))
 specific_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_AVATAR', 'TARGET_X86_64'], if_true: files('configurable_machine.c'))
 specific_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_AVATAR', 'TARGET_PPC'], if_true: files('configurable_machine.c'))
+specific_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_AVATAR', 'TARGET_PPC64'], if_true: files('configurable_machine.c'))
 specific_ss.add(when: ['CONFIG_AVATAR', 'TARGET_SH4'], if_true: files('configurable_machine.c'))
 
